OpenSCAD bootstrap attribution
-------------------------------
The plugin can download a pinned OpenSCAD development snapshot from the
official `files.openscad.org` host when no supported system executable is
available. The exact URLs and SHA-256 digests are checked into
`openscad/bootstrap.py`; the platform-specific OpenSCAD binaries and their
bundled dependencies remain under the OpenSCAD project's licenses and are not
relicensed by this repository. The bootstrap stores the upstream package in a
per-user cache rather than vendoring it here. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.

AI runtime downloads
--------------------
The optional AI feature downloads Node.js v24.21.0 from the official Node.js
release host and installs `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` v0.87.1 from npm at
runtime. Node.js is distributed under the MIT license; its upstream archive
contains its full license and bundled third-party notices. Pi coding agent is
published under the MIT license; its npm package and installed dependencies
retain their respective upstream license files. These runtimes are stored in a
per-user cache and are not vendored in this repository. See
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES for attribution pointers.

Host attribution
